  "content": "The Noble Maitreya's King of AspirationsHomage to all buddhas and bodhisattvas.Ānanda, in the past, when the bodhisattva mahāsattva Maitreya was practicing the conduct of a bodhisattva, three times each day and three times each night, he would adjust his upper robe over one shoulder, rest his right knee on the ground, join his palms, and, making all the buddhas manifest before him, offer this prayer:Homage to all the Buddhas.Homage to the sages who possess the divine eye,To the bodhisattvas,And to the śrāvakas as well.Turning one back from the lower realms,Perfectly showing the path to the higher realms,And leading to the state without aging or death,To this bodhicitta, I pay homage.Because I have fallen under the power of the mind,Whatever misdeeds I have committed,Having come into the presence of the Buddhas,I shall confess them all.Whatever merit has been generatedThrough the three aspects,May it be the seed of my omniscience,And may my enlightenment be inexhaustible.In the realms of the ten directions,Whatever offerings are made to the Buddhas,In which the Buddhas in their wisdom rejoice,In that, I also rejoice.I confess all my misdeeds,I rejoice in all merit,I prostrate to all the Buddhas,And may I attain the supreme primordial wisdom.Throughout the various quarters of the ten directions,To the bodhisattvas dwelling on the ten stages,I offer this exhortationTo attain supreme, enlightened Buddhahood.Having fully awakened into the most sacred enlightenment,And having subdued the Maras along with their hosts,For the sake of benefiting all living beings,May you turn the wheel of Dharma.Through the sound of the great drum of Dharma,May beings in suffering be liberated.Throughout inconceivable tens of millions of eons,May you remain and continue to teach the Dharma.Sunk in the mire of desire,Tightly bound by the cords of craving,I am fettered by every form of bondage;O Supreme among Humans, please look upon me.The Buddhas do not express contemptFor those whose minds have become defiled.Possessing a heart of love for all sentient beings,May they deliver them from the ocean of existence.To all the perfect Buddhas who currently abide,And all those who have passed away or are yet to come,I shall train by following in their footsteps,And may I practice the conduct of enlightenment.Having brought the six perfections to completion,May I bring the sentient beings of the six realms to the final goal.Having actualized the six superknowledges,May I attain unsurpassed enlightenment.Unborn and non-arising,Without intrinsic nature and without location,Without mental representation and without substance,May I realize the phenomena of emptiness.Just like the Buddha, the Great Sage,Without sentient beings, without life-force,Without individuals, without persons,May I realize the dharma of selflessness.Without dwelling upon any entityOf grasping at a self or grasping at \"mine,\"For the sake of benefiting all sentient beings,May I practice generosity without stinginess.Since entities do not exist as entities,May my resources be spontaneously accomplished.Through the total disintegration of all things,May I complete the perfection of generosity.With ethical discipline that is flawless,Endowed with discipline that is utterly pure,Through discipline free from arrogance,May I complete the perfection of ethical discipline.Like the elements of earth, water, fire,Or the element of wind, may I not dwell,And being without patience or anger,May I complete the perfection of patience.Through the diligence of initiated effort,Being stable, enthusiastic, and free from laziness,With a body and mind endowed with strength,May I complete the perfection of diligence.Through the illusion-like samādhi,The samādhi of heroic progress,And the vajra-like samādhi,May I complete the perfection of meditative concentration.Through the three doors of liberation,The equality of the three times,And the realization of the three types of higher knowledge,May I complete the perfection of wisdom.Through the praise of all the Buddhas,The blazing of light and majesty,And the diligence of a Bodhisattva,May my aspirations be fulfilled.Engaging in such practices,And possessing the renown of Maitreya,Having completed the six perfections,May I firmly abide upon the ten stages.Immediately upon passing away from this life,May I be born in Tuṣita with a joyful mind,And having swiftly delighted the Protector Maitreya,May I receive the prophecy of my enlightenment.",
